---
layout: layouts/base.njk
bodyClass: "ind-page"
---
{#
  Layout for the location pages — /ai-training-<location>/.

  Reuses the .ind class family and the same proof, curriculum and support data as
  the industry pages: same product, same funnel job, approached from the other
  direction. A second stylesheet and a second copy of the syllabus would only be
  two more things to keep in step.

  The cross-reference is the point. Each location names the sectors that cluster
  there and links to their page; each industry page names all seven areas. Neither
  has to win "AI training Australia" for the pair to answer "AI training for NDIS
  providers in Logan".

  On presence: the first version of these pages volunteered "we don't have a
  Brisbane office and we're not going to pretend otherwise" in the third
  paragraph, to someone who arrived by searching AI training Brisbane. Being
  accurate about where we sit does not require arguing against the sale — the
  `presence` field now states what we cover, and the Gold Coast base is a fact
  about us rather than an apology.

  Front matter each page supplies:
    title, description, permalink, location, region, slug, h1, eyebrow, lede,
    presence, contextHeading, context, industriesHere, faq, nextStep, closer
#}
<main class="ind">

  <section>
    <p class="ind-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow or ("AI training in " ~ location) }}</p>
    <h1>{{ h1 }}</h1>
    <p class="ind-lede">{{ lede | safe }}</p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-quiz/">Get your free AI audit</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/ai-enquiry/">Or book a time to talk</a>
    </div>
    <p class="ind-trust">
      <b>Trusted by over {{ proof.clientCount }} Australian businesses.</b>
      Australian-owned since {{ proof.since }}, rated {{ proof.rating }} from
      {{ proof.reviewCount }} Google reviews, and delivered by Claude Certified Associates.
    </p>
    <div class="ind-logos" aria-label="Businesses that work with Ad On Group">
      {% for c in proof.clients %}
      <img src="{{ c.src }}" alt="{{ c.name }}" loading="lazy" width="120" height="40">
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if context and context.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>{{ contextHeading or ("Why " ~ location + " businesses are asking") }}</h2>
    {% for c in context %}<p>{{ c | safe }}</p>{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if industriesHere and industriesHere.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>The sectors we see most in {{ location }}</h2>
    <p>
      The program is the same three months wherever you are. What changes is the examples
      and the workflows, which follow the work your team actually does.
    </p>
    <div class="ind-grid">
      {% for ih in industriesHere %}
        {% for i in industries.items %}{% if i.url == ih.url %}
        <article class="ind-card">
          <h3><a href="{{ i.url }}">{{ i.label }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ ih.why | safe }}</p>
        </article>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# The syllabus, same as the industry pages. "What does Ad On Group teach?" has
     to be answerable from any entry point, not just one. #}
  <section>
    <h2>What your team actually learns</h2>
    <p>
      {{ curriculum.moduleCount }} interactive modules over {{ curriculum.duration }},
      {{ curriculum.weeklyHours }} — full of worked examples, videos and step-by-step
      instructions, and they keep growing as the tools do.
    </p>
    <ol class="ind-months">
      {% for m in curriculum.months %}
      <li>
        <p class="ind-mhead"><b>Month {{ m.n }}</b> {{ m.name }} <i>{{ m.tag }}</i></p>
        <p>{{ m.body | safe }}</p>
        <ul class="ind-teaches">
          {% for t in m.teaches %}<li>{{ t }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="{{ curriculum.pdf }}" download>Download the full curriculum</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who teaches it</h2>
    <p>
      Delivered by Claude Certified Associates — not generalists who added an AI workshop
      last year. Ad On Group has been running as an Australian business since
      {{ proof.since }}.
    </p>
    <div class="ind-people">
      {% for t in proof.trainers %}
      <a class="ind-person" href="{{ t.url }}">
        <img src="{{ t.img }}" alt="{{ t.name }}, {{ t.role }}" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120">
        <span><b>{{ t.name }}</b>{{ t.role }}</span>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The part that doesn't stop when the course does</h2>
    <p>
      Every program includes it. This is the difference between a team that had AI training
      once and a team that keeps getting better at it while the tools keep changing.
    </p>
    <div class="ind-features">
      {% for f in proof.support %}
      <figure class="ind-feature">
        <img src="{{ f.img }}" alt="{{ f.alt }}" loading="lazy" width="640" height="380">
        <figcaption><h3>{{ f.title }}</h3><p>{{ f.body | safe }}</p></figcaption>
      </figure>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if proof.aiReviews.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>What people say after the program</h2>
    <div class="ind-reviews">
      {% for r in proof.aiReviews %}{% if loop.index <= 3 %}
      <figure class="ind-review">
        <div class="ind-stars" aria-label="{{ r.rating }} out of 5">★★★★★</div>
        <blockquote>{{ r.text }}</blockquote>
        <figcaption>{{ r.name }}</figcaption>
      </figure>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="ind-trust">Rated {{ proof.rating }} from {{ proof.reviewCount }} Google reviews.</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <div class="ind-note">
      <h2>How we work with {{ location }}</h2>
      <p>{{ presence | safe }}</p>
      {% if deliveryNote %}<p>{{ deliveryNote | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
      <p>
        The program runs online and self-paced, so nobody loses a day travelling to a
        classroom and your team gets exactly what a team down the road from us gets.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="ind-note ind-next">
      <h2>{{ nextStepHeading or "What happens when you get in touch" }}</h2>
      <p>{{ nextStep | safe }}</p>
      <div class="ind-actions">
        <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-quiz/">Get your free AI audit</a>
        <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if faq and faq.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>Questions {{ location }} teams ask</h2>
    {% for item in faq %}
    <details>
      <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
      <div><p>{{ item.a | safe }}</p></div>
    </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>We also train teams in</h2>
    <div class="ind-more">
      {% for l in locations.items %}{% if l.slug != slug %}
        {% if l.hasPage %}<a href="/ai-training-{{ l.slug }}/">{{ l.name }}</a>
        {% else %}<span class="ind-place">{{ l.name }}</span>{% endif %}
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>{{ closerHeading or ("Get your " ~ location + " team started") }}</h2>
    <p>{{ closer | safe }}</p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-quiz/">Get your free AI audit</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
